From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rudraksha Gupta <guptarud@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 08:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rmtfs: Start rmtfs.service when the modem remoteproc appears

With -s, rmtfs exits with "Failed to get rprocfd" when it is started
before the modem remoteproc registers, and systemd gives up after 5
restarts in 10 seconds, so the modem never starts.

Reproduce (Samsung Galaxy Express, MSM8960):

  echo "blacklist qcom_q6v4_mss" > /etc/modprobe.d/late-mss.conf
  printf '[Timer]\nOnBootSec=150\n[Install]\nWantedBy=timers.target\n' > /etc/systemd/system/late-mss.timer
  printf '[Service]\nType=oneshot\nExecStart=/sbin/modprobe qcom_q6v4_mss\n' > /etc/systemd/system/late-mss.service
  systemctl enable late-mss.timer
  reboot
  journalctl -b -u rmtfs
  # Failed to get rprocfd
  # rmtfs.service: Start request repeated too quickly.

rmtfs.rules:

  ACTION!="remove", KERNEL=="qcom_rmtfs_mem*", TAG+="systemd"

    Track /dev/qcom_rmtfs_mem1 as dev-qcom_rmtfs_mem1.device so that
    rmtfs.service can depend on it. It no longer starts rmtfs.service,
    because the memory device can appear before the modem. The tag is
    set on every event instead of only on add, because systemd treats
    the device as gone after a change event that does not set it.

  ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="remoteproc", ATTRS{modalias}=="*-mss-pil*|*-mpss-pas*", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="rmtfs.service"

    Start rmtfs.service when a remoteproc appears whose parent's
    compatible contains -mss-pil or -mpss-pas, the modems that
    rproc_init_by_modalias() looks for.

  ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="remoteproc", DRIVERS=="qcom-q6v5-mss", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="rmtfs.service"

    The same for a remoteproc whose parent uses the qcom-q6v5-mss
    driver, the modems that rproc_init_by_mss_driver() looks for.

  The comment described the old trigger and is removed.

rmtfs.service.in:

  Requires=dev-qcom_rmtfs_mem1.device
  After=dev-qcom_rmtfs_mem1.device

    Replace ConditionPathExists=/dev/qcom_rmtfs_mem1, which skipped
    rmtfs when the memory device was not there yet, with a dependency
    that waits for it.

  [Install] with WantedBy=multi-user.target is removed, so rmtfs is no
  longer started at boot before the modem exists.

Signed-off-by: Rudraksha Gupta <guptarud@gmail.com>
---
 rmtfs.rules      |   13 +++----------
 rmtfs.service.in |    6 ++----
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/rmtfs.rules b/rmtfs.rules
index 33aee0d..ea6bc8f 100644
--- a/rmtfs.rules
+++ b/rmtfs.rules
@@ -1,10 +1,3 @@
-# Trigger rmtfs.service when the qcom_rmtfs_mem device node appears.
-#
-# /dev/qcom_rmtfs_mem* is created by the rmtfs-mem kernel module when the
-# modem shared-memory region is probed.  The exact boot time at which this
-# happens depends on whether the module is built-in or loaded as a module and
-# on the systemd target ordering, so a static ConditionPathExists check in the
-# service unit is not sufficient – the service must be (re-)triggered by udev
-# whenever the device shows up.
-
-ACTION=="add", KERNEL=="qcom_rmtfs_mem*", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="rmtfs.service"
+ACTION!="remove", KERNEL=="qcom_rmtfs_mem*", TAG+="systemd"
+ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="remoteproc", ATTRS{modalias}=="*-mss-pil*|*-mpss-pas*", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="rmtfs.service"
+ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="remoteproc", DRIVERS=="qcom-q6v5-mss", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="rmtfs.service"
diff --git a/rmtfs.service.in b/rmtfs.service.in
index f7df549..f4fdba2 100644
--- a/rmtfs.service.in
+++ b/rmtfs.service.in
@@ -1,12 +1,10 @@
 [Unit]
 Description=Qualcomm remotefs service
 Before=NetworkManager.service
-ConditionPathExists=/dev/qcom_rmtfs_mem1
+Requires=dev-qcom_rmtfs_mem1.device
+After=dev-qcom_rmtfs_mem1.device
 
 [Service]
 ExecStart=RMTFS_PATH/rmtfs -r -P -s
 Restart=always
 RestartSec=1
-
-[Install]
-WantedBy=multi-user.target
-- 
2.39.5

